From 0ed32927b38d69d7ae274a7b14eb38db0dbf675a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 14:45:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] xen/arm: vgic: serialise pci_irq_level[] store under the
 target vCPU lock

The domain-global d->arch.vgic.pci_irq_level[] array (added by the
legacy-PCI level-emulation series, 0013/0019) is written in
vgic_inject_irq() without any lock, while the reader gic_update_one_lr()
reads the same slot under the target vCPU's arch.vgic.lock.  The
unsynchronised store races the LR update: a lost level update (missed
interrupt) or a stale "true" re-injection (spurious interrupt storm).

Take the target vCPU's vgic.lock around the store only, mirroring the
lock the reader uses for the same virq.  vgic_get_target_vcpu() is a
lock-free lookup, so there is no nesting with the injection lock taken
later in the same function.  Behaviour is otherwise unchanged (the
falling-edge early return and the injection path are untouched).

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on the downstream legacy-PCI
 level-emulation series (0013/0019): d->arch.vgic.pci_irq_level[] does not
 exist upstream, so this cannot be submitted as-is]
---
--- a/xen/arch/arm/vgic.c
+++ b/xen/arch/arm/vgic.c
@@ -781,7 +781,20 @@
     if ( virq >= GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_SPI_FIRST &&
          virq < GUEST_VIRTIO_PCI_SPI_LAST &&
          !test_bit(virq, d->arch.vgic.allocated_irqs) )
+    {
+        /*
+         * Serialise the domain-global pci_irq_level[] store against
+         * gic_update_one_lr(), which reads the same slot under the target
+         * vCPU's vgic.lock.  Without this lock the store races the LR update
+         * (lost level update / stale re-injection).
+         */
+        struct vcpu *tv = v ? v : vgic_get_target_vcpu(d->vcpu[0], virq);
+        unsigned long pflags;
+
+        spin_lock_irqsave(&tv->arch.vgic.lock, pflags);
         vgic_pci_irq_level(d, virq) = level;
+        spin_unlock_irqrestore(&tv->arch.vgic.lock, pflags);
+    }
 
     /*
      * For edge triggered interrupts we always ignore a "falling edge".
